{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the patent application drafts against the provided inventor source materials. The review compared every claim limitation, numbered part, and described structure in the draft application with the authoritative disclosure in `input/disclosure.md` and the USER passages of `input/conversation.md`.\n\nThe core invention, including the lid-registered thermal module and the resulting passive circulation path, is well-supported and consistently described across the claims, detailed description, and summary. The optional features, including the condensate management system and the mechanical exposure indicator, are also traced to their source.\n\nHowever, the review identified three instances in the figure briefs (`figures/FIG-1.md` and `figures/FIG-5.md`) where specific geometric or topological details have been introduced that are not explicitly supported by the inventor's disclosure. While these details represent reasonable choices for schematic depiction, they constitute assertions of technical substance that lack a direct source. The findings below detail these discrepancies and provide specific, actionable fixes to align the figure briefs with the source disclosure, thereby ensuring full source fidelity before rendering. No other issues were found."}
